/-!
# The coordinate cut of Stacks Tag 02NP, finished

`Stacks.VeryAmpleAffineBase.ProjCoordinateImmersion` is what the coordinate cut of
[Stacks, Tag 02NP] still owed: from an immersion `α : X ⟶ Proj Γ(S, Sym(E))` over an affine base
carrying the degree-one twist to `L`, a finite family of global sections of `L` whose pinned
morphism `p : X ⟶ ℙⁿ_S` is an immersion. This file proves it, and hence
`Stacks.VeryAmpleAffineBase.ProjCoordinateCut` and [Stacks, Tag 02NP] unconditionally.

## The cut, and why the coordinates are chosen twice

`Stacks.CoordinateChoice` cuts `X` by the charts `α⁻¹(D₊(f_j))` of standard opens of homogeneous
elements of positive degree inside `Scheme.Hom.coborderRange`: there the chart is affine, `α`
restricts to a closed immersion, and the algebra generators over the base are fractions
`b / f_j^{k}`. The morphism to `ℙⁿ_S`, however, is pinned on the charts `α⁻¹(D₊(y_i))` of
*degree-one* coordinates, and those are not affine. The two covers are compared by cutting with
the product `y_i f_j`, whose chart is a cutting chart of the same kind
(`Stacks.OverlapChart`) and which lies inside the coordinate chart.

That forces the coordinates to be chosen **twice**, and the second choice is not a repetition:

1. a first family `y⁰` of degree-one elements in which every `f_j` is a polynomial, so that the
   charts `α⁻¹(D₊(y⁰_i))` already cover `X` and therefore so do the overlap charts
   `α⁻¹(D₊(y⁰_i f_j))`;
2. the algebra generators of each *overlap* chart `α⁻¹(D₊(y⁰_i f_j))`, as fractions
   `b / (y⁰_i f_j)^k` — these exist only once the first family is fixed, since the chart does;
3. the final family `y`, in which every one of those numerators is a polynomial **and which
   contains `y⁰` outright**, by
   `Stacks.CoordinateImmersion.exists_fin_mem_adjoin_range_subset`.

Containment of the first family in the final one is what the cut needs and what
`Stacks.CoordinateChoice.exists_fin_mem_adjoin_range` does not give: the overlap chart
`α⁻¹(D₊(y⁰_i f_j))` has to lie in the *pinning* chart `α⁻¹(D₊(y_{i'}))` of a member of the final
family, which it does exactly when `y⁰_i` is that member.

## Main results

* `Stacks.CoordinateImmersion.exists_fin_mem_adjoin_range_subset`: **the degree-one coordinates,
  chosen to contain a prescribed finite set of degree-one elements.**
* `Stacks.CoordinateImmersion.isClosedImmersion_morphismRestrict_basicOpen_of_eq`: the closed
  immersion over a standard open of the target, with the standard open of the image named by an
  equality of opens rather than written out.
* `Stacks.CoordinateImmersion.mem_closure_overlap`: **the sections of the overlap chart are
  generated by the base sections, the coordinate ratios and one inverse** — the generating set the
  morphism to `ℙⁿ_S` reaches.
* `Stacks.CoordinateImmersion.exists_cuttingSection`: **the cutting section.** A section `t` of
  the chart `D₊(T_i) ⊓ pr⁻¹(⊤)` of `ℙⁿ_S` whose standard open pulls back to the overlap chart and
  over which `p` is a closed immersion.
* `Stacks.CoordinateImmersion.projCoordinateImmersion`:
  **`Stacks.VeryAmpleAffineBase.ProjCoordinateImmersion`.**
* `Stacks.CoordinateImmersion.projCoordinateCut`:
  **`Stacks.VeryAmpleAffineBase.ProjCoordinateCut`.**
* `Stacks.CoordinateImmersion.hasImmersionTwistOver_of_isRelativelyVeryAmple`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 02NP], unconditionally.**

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02NP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02NP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01T2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01T2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01VS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01VS)
-/

